Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:18:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] gfxstream: leave the pool untouched when a batched
 descriptor allocation fails

Validate the whole batch against a scratch copy of the per-type counts and
the free reserved IDs, then commit the counts and the set count at once.
A failed batch returns VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_POOL_MEMORY with every output handle
set to VK_NULL_HANDLE and leaves the live counts and reserved IDs as they
were (previously the counts of the sets before the failing one leaked).

Written by Codex, reviewed and committed by Claude Code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I35b7b3a28d1a9424086b1a5586ff186c221d75ea

